WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:06.400
In commercial Azure, which a G C C
tenant uses, both steps run as written.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.850
As side notes for Azure
Government, check regions first.

4
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:14.074
Learn's comparison page says
Front Door Standard and Premium

5
00:00:14.074 --> 00:00:18.050
are generally available in U S
Gov Arizona and U S Gov Texas.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.600
Front Door Private Link lists
three government regions,

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.529
but the same page limits it to
regions with availability zones,

8
00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:28.852
and Learn's Azure Government
region list shows zones

9
00:00:28.852 --> 00:00:32.025
only in U S Gov Virginia, so
test before relying on it.

10
00:00:32.025 --> 00:00:37.027
Azure Firewall Premium's government
regions are on the products-by-region page,

11
00:00:37.027 --> 00:00:40.513
not Learn, so the guide records
them as not yet specified.

12
00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:44.356
On other clouds, the guide
names O C I Network Firewall,

13
00:00:44.356 --> 00:00:49.422
built on Palo Alto Networks, with
intrusion detection and prevention,

14
00:00:49.422 --> 00:00:54.313
TLS inspection and URL filtering,
reached through V C N route tables.

15
00:00:54.313 --> 00:00:59.710
AWS Network Firewall and Google's
Cloud N G F W aren't compared there.
